From 89073e8af9d74adca34979990f7586e88210fb9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tryinget <markus@team-wangler.de>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 02:53:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/13] fix(host): process every framed stdin message in a
 chunk

The stdin reader parsed frames in a loop, but the EXTENSION_HELLO and
TARGET_EVENT branches returned from the whole function instead of moving
to the next frame. Native messaging delivers several frames per chunk (a
TARGET_EVENT followed by the reply to a tool request is the common case),
so the reply behind such a frame stayed in the buffer until the extension
sent something else: in practice the first request after host start, and
any request whose reply shared a chunk with a tab event, took the full
client timeout (60 s) although the extension had answered in
milliseconds.

Move the framing into native/stdin-frames.cjs (takeFrames/encodeFrame),
drain every complete frame per chunk, and dispatch each one through
handleExtensionFrame, where the early returns are correct. Unit-tested
with multi-frame chunks, split frames and multi-byte payloads.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PpyRJ9kNJBQ5JiqeYjxkTF
